-- title:
--   Transport of level automorphisms along a cyclotomic coefficient map
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a subring $R$ of a field $F$ containing an element $j\neq 0$ the algebra $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,R\,F\,j$ is the set of elements of $F$ integral over $R[j]$ (the integral closure of $R[j]$ in $F$), a subalgebra of $F$.
--
--   **Data over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ and its reduction.** A prime $q$ with $5\le q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ such that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime`). A finite set $W$ of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ — the subfield of the Laurent series field generated over the residue field by the reductions of the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j(M'\tau)$ — is assumed by `hW` to consist exactly of the supersingular places $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'$, i.e. of those places $w$ which are rational (the residue field of $w$ is generated by the constants), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and for which the value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the geometric $j$-generator lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$, the set of those $j$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'\le\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of subfields of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\bar{\mathbb Q}$, the first being generated over $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the divisor expansions of level $M'$, the second the corresponding base change of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` datum for $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$: a valuation subring of the source whose intersection with the constants is $A$, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target whose kernel is the maximal ideal of that subring and which on constants induces the residue map of $A$, a clause producing for each nonzero element a constant scaling it into the subring with nonzero residue, and a degree-preserving map on places compatible with the order functions (ten fields in all, summarised here). The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\bar{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **The constant field and its valuation ring.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\bar{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$. Write $A_0:=A.\mathrm{comap}(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,k_0\,\bar{\mathbb Q})$ for the induced valuation ring of $k_0$. The hypotheses on $A_0$ are: it is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), it is a Henselian local ring (`hhens`), and its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`). The hypothesis `hκ` states that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **The auxiliary prime, roots of unity and the function field over $k_0$.** A prime $\ell'$ with $\ell'\neq q$, $3\le\ell'$ and $\ell'\nmid M'$; an element $\xi\in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity (`hξ`), and the hypothesis `hιξ` that some ring homomorphism $k_0\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. An intermediate field $K$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,k_0$ over $k_0$, which by `hK` equals $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H=\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M'$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$; so $K$ is generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise images of the rational $q$-expansions of that function field. The field $K$ is an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $k_0$, and $j\in K$ is a nonzero element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the standard $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$ of the $j$-function (`hj`).
--
--   **Weierstrass and moduli frame over $A_0$.** Four equivariance and representability hypotheses, for all $A_0$-algebras $T$: `hℓ`, that the predicate $\mathrm{IsLevelPStructure}\,W\,\ell'\,D$ for a level-$\ell'$ datum $D$ (two points on the affine curve with $\mathrm{preΨ}_{\ell'}$ vanishing at their abscissae and both independence elements units) is preserved when $W$ is replaced by $C\bullet W$ and $D$ by $D.\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$; `hM`, that $\mathrm{IsGamma0PowAt}\,W\,p\,k\,h$ — the two-kernel condition if $p^k=2$, otherwise the cyclic-generator-kernel condition on $h$ — is preserved when $W$ is replaced by $C\bullet W$ and $h$ by $\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}\,C\,(\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,k)\,h$; `hVC`, the existence for each projective Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$ and variable change $C$ of a graded ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from $\mathrm{projModelGradingCR}\,W$ to $\mathrm{projModelGradingCR}\,(C\bullet W)$ satisfying the irrelevant-ideal condition and $\mathrm{IsVariableChangeHom}\,W\,C\,\varphi$; and `hCO`, the analogous existence for the coefficient homomorphism attached to an $A_0$-algebra map $f:T\to T'$, with $\mathrm{IsCoefficientHom}$. In addition, a family of relative group laws $\mathcal G$ on the projective models over $A_0$-algebras with $\mathcal G.\mathrm{IsChordTangent}$ and $\mathcal G.\mathrm{IsOriginIdentity}$, and a $\mathrm{LevelTransport}$ datum $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ at $q$ (functorial transport of raw Drinfeld pairs along algebra maps and variable changes, preserving the Drinfeld-level condition) with $\mathcal T.\mathrm{IsSectionTransport}$.
--
--   **The cyclotomic model.** A field $L_1$ of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb Q$ of type $\{q\ell'\}$, with $\zeta_1\in L_1$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity and $\xi_1\in L_1$ a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity; an intermediate field $K_1$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L_1$ over $L_1$ given by the same base change as $K$ but with constants $L_1$ (`hK₁`); a discrete valuation domain $A_1$ with fraction field $L_1$ such that $q$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A_1$ (`hA₁q`) and $\zeta_1$ is in the image of $A_1$ (`hζA₁`); $K_1$ is an $A_1$-algebra compatibly with $L_1$; a nonzero $j_1\in K_1$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of $\mathrm{jq}$ (`hj₁`); a uniformiser $\varpi_1$ of $A_1$ (`hϖ₁`). Further, a point $z_1$ of the two-chart integral model $\mathcal X_1:=\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,A_1\,K_1\,j_1$ (the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j$-finite and $j$-inverse chart algebras along the middle chart), an element $\varpi_{z_1}$ of the stalk of $\mathcal X_1$ at $z_1$ which by `hϖz₁` is the image of $\varpi_1$ under the global-sections map of the structure morphism $\mathcal X_1\to\operatorname{Spec}A_1$ followed by the germ at $z_1$, and `hz₁`, that $\varpi_{z_1}$ lies in the maximal ideal of that stalk; a point $y_1$ of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_1\,K_1\,j_1$ mapping to $z_1$ under the canonical morphism (`hy₁`); and `hss₁`, the supersingularity of $y_1$: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_1\,K_1\,j_1$ to $\Omega$ with kernel the prime $y_1$, the value $\varphi(\mathrm{jChartFin})$ lies in $\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\Omega$.
--
--   **The comparison map.** A ring homomorphism $\iota:L_1\to k_0$ with $\iota(\xi_1)=\xi$ (`hιξ₁`), carrying $A_1$ into $A$ in the sense that the image in $\bar{\mathbb Q}$ of $\iota(\mathrm{algebraMap}\,a)$ lies in $A$ for all $a\in A_1$ (`hιA`), and with the converse property that any $x\in L_1$ whose image lies in $A$ already comes from $A_1$ (`hιA'`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every $\gamma\in SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ belonging to $\Gamma_0(M')$, every $L_1$-algebra automorphism $\tau_1$ of $K_1$ satisfying $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,L_1\,(q\ell')\,\xi_1\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K_1\,\tau_1$, and every proof $\mathrm{hpres}_1$ that $\tau_1$ maps $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_1\,K_1\,j_1$ into itself, there exist a ring homomorphism
--   $$c:\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_1\,K_1\,j_1\longrightarrow\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j,$$
--   an automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ over $k_0$, a proof of $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,k_0\,(q\ell')\,\xi\,(q\ell')\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\,\gamma^{-1}\,K\,\tau$, and a proof $\mathrm{hpres}$ that $\tau$ maps $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ into itself, such that both of the following hold: first, for every $a$ in $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_1\,K_1\,j_1$ the Laurent series over $k_0$ underlying $c(a)$ is obtained from the Laurent series over $L_1$ underlying $a$ by applying $\iota$ to each coefficient; and second, the restriction of $\tau$ to $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ composed after $c$ equals $c$ composed after the restriction of $\tau_1$ to $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_1\,K_1\,j_1$, that is, the square formed by $c$ and the two restricted automorphisms commutes.
--
--   Here the level-automorphism condition $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\,L\,n\,\zeta\,m\,N_0\,H\,\gamma\,K\,\tau$ says: for every weight $k\in\mathbb Z$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for the group $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ (viewed in $GL(2,\mathbb R)$) whose $q$-expansions are the images of integral power series $p_f,p_g$, with the Laurent series attached to $p_g$ over $\mathbb Q$ nonzero, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the quotient of those two Laurent series, and every ring homomorphism $\iota_0:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota_0(\zeta)=\exp(2\pi i/n)$, the coefficientwise $\iota_0$-image of the Laurent series of $\tau x$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\gamma$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\gamma$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}\,m\,\gamma$ is the matrix $\begin{pmatrix}a&b/m\\ mc&d\end{pmatrix}$ for $\gamma=\begin{pmatrix}a&b\\ c&d\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   This is a transport step for the modular curve $X_H$ of level $(q\ell')^2M'$: the coefficientwise extension $\iota$ of the cyclotomic base field to the constant field $k_0$ is realised on the $j$-finite integral chart algebras, and the automorphism of $K_1$ implementing $\gamma^{-1}$ on $q$-expansions is matched with one of $K$ implementing the same slash operation, compatibly with the chart algebras. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_ringHom_chartAlgFin_levelAut_comap_eq_of_isLevelAutAt_of_ringHom_cyclotomic_rigidDataPow`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_ringHom_chartAlgFin_levelAut_comap_eq_of_isLevelAutAt_of_ringHom_cyclotomic_rigidDataPow), where the comparison is needed to move semistability and supersingularity data from the cyclotomic model over $A_1$ to the model over the valuation ring of $k_0$.
